# Repo-root .gitignore — AURA Hub website (Vite + React)
# (Replaces the historical static-site file, which covered only OS/editor
# files and did not ignore node_modules/, dist/ or .wrangler/.)

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Editor ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Dependencies (never commit) ---
node_modules/

# --- Build output (regenerated by `npm run build`) ---
dist/

# --- Cloudflare / Wrangler local state ---
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

# --- Local environment files ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

# --- Logs ---
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# NOTE (deployment exclusion, formerly .assetsignore):
# The old static site served the repo root (wrangler assets directory "./")
# and relied on .assetsignore to keep .git, .wrangler, .github,
# node_modules, wrangler.jsonc, .gitignore and .assetsignore itself out of
# uploads. The v2 build serves ./dist only, so upload exclusion is structural:
# only files Vite copies from public/ plus built assets can ever upload.
# No separate .assetsignore file is needed. If defense-in-depth is wanted, an
# .assetsignore containing "node_modules" is harmless but has no effect when
# the assets directory is ./dist.
#
# Intentionally NOT ignored here: tmp/, tmp-verify/, *.md drafts.
# They are human review artifacts; decide to commit or delete explicitly.
